# Releases

Follow the [shared release policy](https://github.com/serrja/baseRules/blob/main/docs/releases.md):
compatibility decision, canonical version and changelog, `make ci-local`, review,
checked main commit, then an explicitly authorized annotated `v<version>` tag.
Inspect workflows before sending one tag; do not rewrite published tags. A missing
or billing-blocked mandatory hosted check prevents merge and tagging.

`make release-check` verifies source-bound build metadata without publication.
A release candidate workflow, when enabled, is manual. Registry publication and
deployment require their own configured destination and authorization. Preserve
prior artifacts and assess database compatibility before a rollback.
